{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And you shall do no manner of work — for it is the Day of Atonement.</b> For on such a day it is fitting to turn away from all other pursuits, so as to give one's heart to attaining forgiveness and atonement — the opposite of ״הֵן בְּיוֹם צוֹמְכֶם תִּמְצְאוּ חֵפֶץ וְכָל עַצְּבֵיכֶם תִּנְגֹּשׂוּ״ (Isaiah 58:3). And since most who sin regarding affliction do so only out of appetite, while most who sin by doing work sin to provoke, therefore the punishment of excision is upon one who does not afflict himself, while the punishment of destruction of the soul is upon one who does work."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:35.433951317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}